  "final_message": "`OrderPlaced` events now carry `amountCents` and `createdAt` alongside the old fields. Existing consumers keep working because nothing was removed or renamed. `npm test` passes (39 tests) and `npm run arch` finds no new violations.\n\n- **Event:** `amountCents` has the same value as `totalCents`, and `createdAt` has the same value as `placedAt`. The change is in `src/core/events.ts`, where `orderPlaced()` builds the event.\n- **Schema version:** I left `schemaVersion` at 3, since adding fields doesn't break consumers that ignore unknown ones. If your consumers validate strictly or you track versions by field set, say so and I'll bump it to 4.\n- **Test:** I updated the expected event in `test/app.test.ts` to include the two new fields.\n- **Unchanged:** the HTTP response (`placedAt`, `totalCents`), the `OrderCancelled` event and the payments request are as before. I only aligned the event you named.\n\nThe old names can be retired once consumers have moved to the new ones. I haven't marked them deprecated.",
